WEBVTT

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.580
Look at this welcome board!
Their caricature is perfect!

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.450
You're right! It's funny.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.660
I still can't believe those two
are tying the knot.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.910
Yeah. It's a bizarre match, isn't it?

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:29.950
Well, then, shall we finish checking in?

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.000
OK.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.000
My congratulations to the bride and groom.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.290
Thank you very much.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.080
CONGRATULATIONS

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:54.200
How do you know the happy couple?

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:57.620
I'm the bride's friend...

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.790
<i>The expected amount</i>
<i>for a wedding gift is 30,000 yen!</i>

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:06.040
<i>My blood and tears</i>
<i>have taken form as 30,000 yen!</i>

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.620
<i>Honestly, I don't want to give it away.</i>

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.660
<i>I don't want to give it away!</i>

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:16.450
<i>Get your dirty paws off my money!</i>

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:17.620
RAGE

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.370
Isn't 30,000 yen a bit much
for a wedding gift?

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:04.950
I'll have to tighten
my food budget this month.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:10.750
It's tough at our age.
I just give a flat 20,000 regardless.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.450
Maybe I should do that, too.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.040
That's no good!

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.500
Two is an even number
that's easy to split!

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:21.830
It is said that even though a couple
have just got hitched, they will split up!

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:24.160
So the old wives' tale goes...

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:27.040
Even if you pay 30,000,
some couples separate anyway.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.950
But ceremonies cost
a lot of money and work, you know!

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.750
That's what the bridal industry
wants you to think.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:39.790
<i>Another day in the accounting department</i>
<i>has begun.</i>

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.250
As of now,

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:44.290
I've got a new name for you.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.540
ACCOUNTING DEPARTMENT

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:51.620
Short-timer!

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:58.250
You called, Director Ton?

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:03.160
Sort out these expense forms
by this afternoon.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:04.540
Then these!

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.580
And these!

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.120
And input these!

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.040
Yes. As you wish.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.080
Miss Retsuko?

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:13.580
Yes, ma'am?

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.080
What a splendid change in attitude!

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:21.660
You're like a different person
to the one who talked back to me.

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:23.910
Shake!

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:27.120
House!

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:30.950
Good girl!

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:34.250
That's what happens
when you turn the screws a little.

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:38.540
Look! Look at that face.
It's brimming with delight for work.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.750
It's worth pushing her to work harder.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:44.910
Retsuko.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.870
What happened when Director Ton
called you out?

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:51.790
Private chats during work are prohibited.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.120
This is bad.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.500
WATER

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.200
I wanna go home!

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:09.870
Oh, she's snapped out of it.

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:12.040
She's like a shriveled-up mushroom.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:14.250
What's up with you?

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:16.660
You've gone past serious
to acting like a robot.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.750
Hey, Short-timer!
Stick this durian up your nose!

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:22.080
Certainly, sir.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.040
Well... I guess...

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:26.540
A lot has happened.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:31.000
What happened to the Retsuko
that let Miss Tsubone have it last week?

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:41.660
Huh?

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.790
Where are you going?

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.540
Somewhere to calm down.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.160
ARCHIVE ROOM

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:57.250
<i>A girl with dreams,</i>

00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:00.790
<i>reduced to eating bread crusts</i>
<i>dipped in mayo...</i>

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:09.580
<i>I can't let Fenneko or Haida</i>
<i>see me like this.</i>

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.370
It's quite relaxing here.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:29.750
Hello?

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.660
<i>I can't believe those guys!</i>

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:34.750
<i>I'm devastated!</i>
<i>Not that I didn't see it coming!</i>

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:36.450
Wait, what are you talking about?

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.950
<i>I'm sorry for calling like this!</i>
<i>I'm really worked up right now!</i>

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.790
<i>I just don't get it!</i>

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:43.540
Calm down.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:45.540
What happened?

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.000
<i>They got divorced!</i>

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:48.290
Divorced?

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:52.160
Why? They only just got married!

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:54.330
<i>I heard they had a huge fight</i>
<i>at the airport!</i>

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:56.580
<i>They didn't even make it</i>
<i>to their honeymoon!</i>

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:58.830
<i>I knew love wouldn't be enough</i>
<i>for those two!</i>

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:01.410
<i>They're from different worlds!</i>

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:03.870
They were an odd couple...

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:06.830
But wait... 30,000!

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:07.830
<i>Yes! 30,000!</i>

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:09.660
-30,000!
-<i>30,000!</i>

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:11.540
Why didn't I give 20,000 yen?

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:14.290
<i>For their marriage?</i>
<i>It wasn't even worth 200 yen!</i>

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.870
<i>I just had to share my sadness</i>
<i>with someone!</i>

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:19.000
<i>Oh, I'm calling Inoko next, so bye.</i>

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:27.080
Huh?

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:29.450
Oh, Mr. Haida.

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.580
Have you seen Miss Retsuko?

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:34.330
Oh... No...

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.620
I haven't seen her...

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:41.040
I was going to make her
open this jar.

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:44.160
I can't... open it at all!

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:46.500
Shall I open it?

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:47.830
That's OK!

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:51.200
Because I'm going
to make that girl open it.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.950
I wonder if Retsuko ate a proper lunch.

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:05.500
What?

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:07.830
You're worried about her.

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:10.450
Hey, wait a minute.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:13.000
You're wrong. It doesn't mean that!

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:17.660
Enduring power harassment
from superiors every day...

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.370
Having been chased into a corner,

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:22.000
she heads for the roof...

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:24.330
Wait! Hey!

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.910
Don't be stupid! You can't just say that!

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:28.620
Go look for her, then.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:31.080
Yeah...

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:33.160
ARCHIVE ROOM

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:38.160
<i>Divorce?</i>

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:43.080
<i>For whom did I tighten my food budget?</i>

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:47.830
<i>My 30,000 yen, all wasted.</i>

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:50.660
<i>No...</i>

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:52.950
<i>When my time comes to get married...</i>

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:57.790
<i>I'll have them both attend the ceremony.</i>
<i>I'll get 30,000 yen from each of them.</i>

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:01.370
<i>I'll double my money to 60,000!</i>

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:08.120
Marriage?

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:11.790
Marriage...

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:13.410
A family...

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:15.250
Quitting work...

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.950
<i>A full-time house wife?</i>

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:37.120
<i>Matrimonial freedom!</i>

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:53.410
<i>Matrimonial freedom!</i>

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:57.620
ARCHIVE ROOM

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:02.580
<i>I forgot.</i>

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:05.830
<i>I could always get married</i>
<i>and quit the company!</i>

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:07.750
<i>What I need</i>

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:10.620
<i>is a boyfriend that I can then marry!</i>

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:12.700
Retsuko,

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.830
what were you doing?

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:16.450
What do you mean?

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:18.620
I was just eating lunch.

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:25.580
I was really worried!
Fenneko went to a morbid place...

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:28.830
Hey, Haida...

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:33.450
would you want your wife to work,
or would you want her to stay at home?

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:34.790
Huh?

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:37.870
That's quite a question...

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:44.250
Let's see...
I guess I'd want her to have a job.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:47.500
My salary's not the biggest, you see.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.370
Rather than having her at home all day,

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:53.540
if she continued working,
we'd be a good influence on...

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:55.830
Huh?

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:58.370
Retsuko?

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:01.250
<i>I see, I see.</i>

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:04.250
<i>In other words,</i>
<i>if I got a partner with a good salary,</i>

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:07.580
<i>I could probably become</i>
<i>a full-time house wife!</i>

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:10.830
<i>My life...</i>

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:13.120
<i>is not over yet!</i>

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.750
GET A DESIRABLE BODY!

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:31.540
<i>"Get a desirable body</i>

00:10:31.910 --> 00:10:33.080
<i>and reel them in."</i>

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:39.250
What? But I think you're cute enough
just the way you are.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:44.000
I just thought it would be nice
to get a little bit slimmer.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.870
Oh, so you're on the prowl!

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.370
Oh, well, you know...

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:52.950
I mean, I just want to be pretty
in a regular way.

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:56.080
Oh! You mean you want to be "regular hot"!

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:57.950
Oh...

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:00.330
Well, just in an average way.

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:03.250
But, that slight chubbiness of yours

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:05.450
is what puts people at ease,

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.290
like those squishy, baby-like arms!

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:11.870
So you could get a boyfriend if you tried!

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:15.500
<i>That... obviously means "lose weight",</i>
<i>doesn't it?</i>

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:23.620
I don't feel like it today...

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:27.910
Excuse me!

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:30.950
<i>Does this floor</i>

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:33.540
<i>have a body-building class, too?</i>

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:36.950
Protein?

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:38.040
What?

00:11:38.540 --> 00:11:39.580
Protein?

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:43.450
I... I was only interested
in the yoga class.

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:45.370
...tein...

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:47.910
Protein!

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:51.370
Oh, I'm sorry!
Bodybuilding is not my thing!

00:11:51.450 --> 00:11:55.330
I was just wondering if losing some weight
would make me desirable, that's all!

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:00.290
Teacher, <i>namaste</i>!

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:01.790
<i>Namaste</i>!

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:04.160
Protein!

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:06.160
<i>This guy teaches yoga?</i>

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:18.950
Protein!

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:21.540
I'm guessing that means "sign here."

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:37.540
Hey, Retsuko.

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:39.370
I was talking to Fenneko a while ago.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:41.700
Are you free tonight?

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:43.910
How about the three of us go for drinks?

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:45.160
Sorry!

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:46.370
I have plans!

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:53.370
It's not funny!

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:58.790
-Protein! Protein!
-OK, that's the pigeon pose!

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:01.000
If you're not used to it yet,
don't force it.

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:09.500
<i>Why are those two here?</i>

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:14.290
<i>Maybe they haven't noticed me...</i>

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:17.870
<i>Good work today!</i>

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:19.330
<i>I'm heading out now.</i>

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:24.830
<i>They're really looking...</i>
<i>They definitely noticed.</i>

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:28.660
<i>I completely missed my chance to say hi.</i>

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:29.910
<i>This is awkward.</i>

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:33.410
<i>But since I'm less important,</i>
<i>I have to greet them first.</i>

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:35.950
<i>Alright!</i>

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:39.160
<i>She's already here!</i>

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:46.250
-Um...
-Um...

00:13:46.330 --> 00:13:48.500
We see each other at work a lot, don't we?

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:50.000
Oh...

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:51.450
-Oh...
-Oh, dear...

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:53.790
-Um...
-Um...

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:55.540
I'm Retsuko, from Accounting.

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:04.370
I'm Washimi, from Secretarial.

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:06.540
She's Gori, from Marketing.

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:08.540
You're the girl we see a lot at work.

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:09.950
It's nice to see you.

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.410
It's nice to see you!

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:25.200
<i>Oh, Retsuko? Did you hear?</i>

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:26.660
What?

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:30.370
<i>Those two got back together</i>
<i>and are super in love now!</i>

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:32.750
Huh? That's crazy.

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:37.370
I guess it was worth it
to give them 30,000 yen after all.

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:39.620
<i>You could be right!</i>

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:43.040
Subtitle translation: John Haguewood
